{"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"toolu_01GgQBxXb3sHDB86HH9t5crW","result":"<file path=\"/Users/andres.mesa/.coda/skills/analyze-context-pack-inputs/references/phase-a-input-discovery-extraction.md\" lines=\"106\" start=\"1\" end=\"106\" returned=\"106\" has_more=\"false\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|# analyze-context-pack-inputs — Phase A: Input Discovery & Source Extraction\n     2|\n     3|## Context Contract\n     4|\n     5|- **Inputs:** `{base_path}/artifacts/inputs/` (source-code archives/dirs, documentation PDFs/MD, transcripts); `meeting-analysis.md` if `transcribe-meetings` ran; the bundled scripts in `scripts/`.\n     6|- **Outputs:** `{OUTPUT_ANALYSIS}/_extractions/{basename}.md` (one distilled file per input); a `SOURCE_LOG` of `raw_source → extraction` pairs carried in working state.\n     7|- **Carries Forward:** the extraction file paths and `SOURCE_LOG` into Phase B; `_progress.json` remains `RUNNING`.\n     8|- **Flush After:** raw source contents — after extraction, Phase B reads `_extractions/*.md` only (§10.2). Never re-read raw sources in Phase B.\n     9|- **Dependency:** FIRST ACTION (§2) `_progress.json` write and §4 Memory Bank Session Start must be done.\n    10|- **H1 Title:** n/a (this phase writes extraction files, not the analysis spec).\n    11|\n    12|## Mode-Specific Behavior\n    13|\n    14|- **BUILD:** Enumerate all inputs, extract archives/PDFs, run the §10.2 extraction pass for every source.\n    15|- **REPAIR:** Reuse existing `_extractions/{basename}.md` when the source is unchanged since the prior run (log `reused extraction: {path}` to SOURCE_LOG). Only re-extract sources named by a repair directive or whose bytes changed.\n    16|- **RESUME:** If `_progress.json` shows extractions already written, skip the extraction pass for those sources and proceed to Phase B for the first `pending` section.\n    17|\n    18|---\n    19|\n    20|## 1. Input discovery\n    21|\n    22|Enumerate `{base_path}/artifacts/inputs/` recursively and categorize by type:\n    23|\n    24|- `artifacts/inputs/source-code/` — `*.zip` archives or already-extracted code directories.\n    25|- `artifacts/inputs/documentation/` — `*.pdf` and `*.md` files.\n    26|- `artifacts/inputs/meetings/` — `*.mp4` files: **skip here.** They are handled by the `transcribe-meetings` skill, whose output (`meeting-analysis.md`) is folded in during Phase B when present.\n    27|\n    28|If a category has no files, note it in the eventual `## Source Summary` and continue. If\n    29|`artifacts/inputs/` is empty overall, the SKILL.md STOP-GATE applies — write a Gap Report and EXIT (§9).\n    30|\n    31|## 2. Preparing source files (bundled scripts)\n    32|\n    33|Both scripts are co-located in this skill's `scripts/` directory, use only the Python\n    34|standard library, and degrade gracefully.\n    35|\n    36|**ZIP archives** (`scripts/unzip_safe.py` — includes zip-slip path-traversal protection):\n    37|\n    38|```bash\n    39|python3 scripts/unzip_safe.py extract \\\n    40|  --input artifacts/inputs/source-code/<archive>.zip \\\n    41|  --output artifacts/inputs/source-code/<archive>/\n    42|```\n    43|\n    44|If Python 3 is unavailable, fall back to the system `unzip`:\n    45|`unzip <archive>.zip -d <archive>/`.\n    46|\n    47|**PDF text** (`scripts/read_pdf.py` — tries `pdfminer.six`, then `pdftotext`, then raw\n    48|binary text extraction):\n    49|\n    50|```bash\n    51|# Extract text\n    52|python3 scripts/read_pdf.py extract-text \\\n    53|  --input artifacts/inputs/documentation/<file>.pdf \\\n    54|  --output artifacts/outputs/context-pack-analysis/<file>-text.md\n    55|\n    56|# Optional: metadata only (title, author, page count)\n    57|python3 scripts/read_pdf.py read-metadata \\\n    58|  --input artifacts/inputs/documentation/<file>.pdf\n    59|```\n    60|\n    61|If neither `pdfminer.six` nor `pdftotext` is available, the script extracts raw readable\n    62|text; note the degraded fidelity in `## Open Questions` and advise `pip install\n    63|pdfminer.six`. For `*.md` files, read directly — no script needed.\n    64|\n    65|---\n    66|\n    67|## 3. Source Extraction Pass (apply execution-protocol.md §10.2)\n    68|\n    69|**Trigger (verbatim from §10.2).** Run the extraction pass if ANY of:\n    70|- More than 2 source files, OR\n    71|- Any single source file > 200 lines, OR\n    72|- Cumulative source content > 500 lines.\n    73|\n    74|If none hold (small bounded input), SKIP the pass and read sources directly in Phase B.\n    75|\n    76|**Mechanism.** `mkdir -p {OUTPUT_ANALYSIS}/_extractions/`. For each input, distill it into\n    77|`{OUTPUT_ANALYSIS}/_extractions/{basename}.md` as ONE fielded bullet-list block using this\n    78|skill's extraction schema. Put a `line: {N}` provenance marker on every entry (for PDFs,\n    79|use the page/`-text.md` line; for binaries, cite the file). Consult\n    80|`input-signal-catalog.md` for which signals map to which context-pack file.\n    81|\n    82|```\n    83|tech_signals:   [{ signal, evidence, line }]        # frameworks, runtimes, deps, versions, DBs, messaging\n    84|domain_terms:   [{ term, definition_or_usage, line }]\n    85|standards:      [{ area: coding|arch|test|security|automation, rule, line }]\n    86|constraints:    [{ constraint, source, line }]       # compliance, hosting, geography, perf, org limits\n    87|infra:          [{ item, detail, line }]             # cloud providers/regions, IaC, containers, networking\n    88|commands:       [{ purpose: build|test|lint|typecheck|security, command, line }]\n    89|inventory:      [{ project_or_type, path, role, line }]   # projects, namespaces, key types, bounded contexts\n    90|open_questions: [{ question, why }]                  # gaps, unparseable files, ambiguities\n    91|```\n    92|\n    93|**Zero Invention (§10.2).** Extraction is distillation, not invention. Facts absent from\n    94|the source do not appear. Inferred industry-standard hints stay tagged `[INFERRED]` in the\n    95|extraction and become `## Open Questions` entries in Phase B — never silent facts.\n    96|\n    97|**After the pass.** Phase B reads `_extractions/*.md` only. The audit's provenance chain is\n    98|`raw_source → extraction → analysis-section`, so keep the SOURCE_LOG complete (including\n    99|`reused extraction` entries in REPAIR).\n   100|\n   101|## 4. Post-phase protocol\n   102|\n   103|- Verify each `_extractions/{basename}.md` exists and is non-empty.\n   104|- Update `_progress.json` (`items[]` or a note that extraction is complete); keep status `RUNNING`.\n   105|- Flush raw source contents from working memory. Proceed to Phase B (`phase-b-analysis-section-generation.md`).\n   106|\n</file>","isError":false}}
