{"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"toolu_01RwSee9bPy3S2vy5d95ZTNL","result":"<file path=\"/Users/andres.mesa/.coda/skills/analyze-context-pack-inputs/references/phase-b-analysis-section-generation.md\" lines=\"165\" start=\"1\" end=\"165\" returned=\"165\" has_more=\"false\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|# analyze-context-pack-inputs — Phase B: Analysis Section Generation\n     2|\n     3|## Context Contract\n     4|\n     5|- **Inputs:** `{OUTPUT_ANALYSIS}/_extractions/*.md` (or raw sources if §10.2 was skipped); `meeting-analysis.md` when present; the mapping tables in `input-signal-catalog.md`.\n     6|- **Outputs:** `{OUTPUT_ANALYSIS}/analysis.md` — one multi-section spec, one section populated per `Edit`.\n     7|- **Carries Forward:** `_progress.json.sections.{name}` flips to `complete` after each section; `skeleton_written: true` after Phase A.\n     8|- **Flush After:** each populated section's body — drop it from working memory before the next section (§10.4). Re-read `SPEC_FILE` only for the two consolidator sections below.\n     9|- **Dependency:** Phase A (extraction pass) COMPLETE.\n    10|- **H1 Title:** `# Context Pack Input Analysis`.\n    11|\n    12|## Mode-Specific Behavior\n    13|\n    14|- **BUILD:** Write the skeleton (§10.3), then populate every section in template order (§10.4).\n    15|- **REPAIR:** Load existing `analysis.md` from the SAME path. Apply only sections named by a repair directive; rewrite those in place; preserve untargeted sections verbatim. Bump the header version; log the delta to the audit.\n    16|- **RESUME / CONTINUE (§10.6):** If `_progress.json` shows `skeleton_written: true` with a partial `sections` map, resume from the first `pending` section. Do not rewrite the skeleton.\n    17|\n    18|---\n    19|\n    20|## Phase A — Skeleton first (§10.3)\n    21|\n    22|Within 5 tool calls, `Write` `SPEC_FILE` with the `# Context Pack Input Analysis` header\n    23|plus one stub per section (heading + `status: pending - will be generated`, **ASCII hyphen\n    24|only**). Flip `_progress.json.skeleton_written: true`. Do not populate yet.\n    25|\n    26|## Phase B — Populate one section per `Edit` (§10.4)\n    27|\n    28|Section list, in template order (each maps to a downstream context-pack file; see\n    29|`input-signal-catalog.md`):\n    30|\n    31|```\n    32|for-domain → for-arch-standards → for-tech-policy → for-coding-standards →\n    33|for-automation-standards → for-test-standards → for-security → for-constraints →\n    34|for-customer-background → for-env-config-and-config-management →\n    35|for-best-practices → for-infrastructure → for-validation-tools →\n    36|for-project-inventory → for-codebase-map → source-summary → open-questions\n    37|```\n    38|\n    39|### Per-section content rules\n    40|\n    41|Populate each section from the extraction fields that feed it. Template:\n    42|\n    43|```markdown\n    44|# Context Pack Input Analysis\n    45|\n    46|## For domain.md\n    47|### Domain Terms and Entities\n    48|<business concepts, entity names, domain rules, bounded contexts found>\n    49|### Business Rules and Invariants\n    50|<rules that govern domain behavior>\n    51|\n    52|## For arch-standards.md\n    53|### Architecture Patterns Observed\n    54|<layering, module structure, integration patterns>\n    55|### Architecture Anti-Patterns Found\n    56|<violations or patterns to avoid>\n    57|\n    58|## For tech-policy.md\n    59|### Tech Stack Detected\n    60|<languages, frameworks, runtimes, databases, messaging>\n    61|### Approved Libraries and Versions\n    62|<dependency list with versions>\n    63|### Prohibited or Deprecated Dependencies\n    64|<anything flagged deprecated or to avoid>\n    65|\n    66|## For coding-standards.md\n    67|### Naming Conventions\n    68|### Code Organization Rules\n    69|### Linting and Formatting Config\n    70|### Error Handling and Logging Patterns\n    71|\n    72|## For automation-standards.md\n    73|### CI/CD Pipeline Details\n    74|### Test Automation Framework\n    75|\n    76|## For test-standards.md\n    77|### Testing Approach\n    78|### Test Frameworks and Patterns\n    79|\n    80|## For security.md\n    81|### Security Patterns Found\n    82|### Security Gaps or Risks\n    83|\n    84|## For constraints.md\n    85|### Hard Constraints Found\n    86|### Known Organizational Limits\n    87|\n    88|## For customer-background.md\n    89|### Customer Context\n    90|\n    91|## For env-config.md and config-management-rules.md\n    92|### Environment Configuration\n    93|### Secret and Config Management\n    94|\n    95|## For best-practices.md\n    96|### General Best Practices Observed\n    97|\n    98|## For infrastructure.md\n    99|### Infrastructure Topology\n   100|### Infrastructure-as-Code Tooling\n   101|### Deployment Targets and Environments\n   102|\n   103|## For validation-tools.md\n   104|### Build Commands\n   105|### Test Commands\n   106|### Lint and Format Commands\n   107|### Typecheck Commands\n   108|### Security Scan Commands\n   109|### Pre-commit and CI Validation Order\n   110|\n   111|## For project-inventory.md\n   112|### Naming Conventions and Patterns\n   113|### Project and Bounded Context Inventory\n   114|### Key Types per Bounded Context\n   115|### Build and Test Commands\n   116|### Domain to Path Lookup\n   117|### Stable Invariants\n   118|\n   119|## For codebase-map.md\n   120|### Solution Structure\n   121|### Bounded Contexts in Scope\n   122|### Layer Conventions\n   123|### Cross-BC Integration Patterns\n   124|### Frontend Layout\n   125|### Test Layout\n   126|### Where to Look for X\n   127|\n   128|## Source Summary\n   129|<brief description of each input file analyzed, with its extraction path>\n   130|\n   131|## Open Questions\n   132|<consolidated gaps, [INFERRED] assumptions, unparseable inputs — see below>\n   133|```\n   134|\n   135|### Cross-section dependency graph\n   136|\n   137|- All `for-*` sections are **independent** — each reads only its own extraction fields; do\n   138|  NOT read `SPEC_FILE` for them.\n   139|- `source-summary` reads the `SOURCE_LOG` from Phase A (raw → extraction pairs).\n   140|- `open-questions` is a **consolidator**: read `SPEC_FILE` to gather every `pending` and\n   141|  `[INFERRED]`/`assumption` item across the populated sections, plus the extraction\n   142|  `open_questions` fields. This is the only section (besides source-summary) that reads\n   143|  prior state (§10.4).\n   144|\n   145|### Zero Invention + Status Protocol (applied per section)\n   146|\n   147|- Every extracted item is `complete` (evidence + provenance captured), `pending` (no\n   148|  evidence — emit the section with `status: pending — no evidence in inputs`), or\n   149|  `assumption` (`[INFERRED]` inline). Assumptions and pendings are mirrored into\n   150|  `## Open Questions`.\n   151|- Never upgrade an `[INFERRED]` hint to a stated fact. Facts absent from the extractions do\n   152|  not appear.\n   153|- **Per-section source-fidelity check before each `Edit`:** confirm every claim in the\n   154|  section body maps to an extraction entry with a `line:` provenance marker. If a claim has\n   155|  no source, either drop it or downgrade it to an `[INFERRED]` assumption. No claim without\n   156|  a source survives the write.\n   157|\n   158|### Tool discipline\n   159|\n   160|Skeleton via `Write`; sections via `Edit` (one section per call). **Never** `Bash` +\n   161|`sed`/`awk`/`python3 <<EOF`/`cat >` to mutate `SPEC_FILE` (§10.5). If any extraction or\n   162|input contains a codepoint > 127 (non-English content is common), apply the §10.5.1\n   163|full-file-`Write` fallback for every section this run. After each section: flip\n   164|`_progress.json.sections.{name}: complete`, then flush the section body from memory.\n   165|\n</file>","isError":false}}
