{"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"toolu_01K1fkUHs91MspNUMXgsxJiD","result":"<file path=\"/Users/andres.mesa/.coda/skills/analyze-context-pack-inputs/references/input-signal-catalog.md\" lines=\"55\" start=\"1\" end=\"55\" returned=\"55\" has_more=\"false\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|# analyze-context-pack-inputs — Input Signal Catalog\n     2|\n     3|## Context Contract\n     4|\n     5|- **Inputs:** the categorized inputs from Phase A (extracted source directories; PDF/MD text).\n     6|- **Outputs:** none directly — this is the lookup catalog Phase A's extraction pass and Phase B's section population consult to route each observed signal to the correct `analysis.md` section / downstream context-pack file.\n     7|- **Carries Forward:** nothing — reference-only.\n     8|- **Flush After:** n/a (read on demand).\n     9|- **Dependency:** none.\n    10|- **H1 Title:** n/a.\n    11|\n    12|Use these tables to decide which extraction field / `analysis.md` section a given observed\n    13|signal feeds. They define the coverage contract between raw inputs and the 17 downstream\n    14|context-pack files.\n    15|\n    16|## Source Code Analysis\n    17|\n    18|For each extracted directory in `artifacts/inputs/source-code/`:\n    19|\n    20|| What to look for | Where to find it | Maps to context-pack file |\n    21||-----------------|-----------------|--------------------------|\n    22|| Tech stack, frameworks, runtime | `package.json`, `pom.xml`, `go.mod`, `requirements.txt`, `Gemfile`, `*.csproj`, `Dockerfile` | `tech-policy.md` |\n    23|| Approved libraries and versions | Dependency manifests | `tech-policy.md` |\n    24|| Linting and formatting rules | `.eslintrc`, `.prettierrc`, `checkstyle.xml`, `.editorconfig`, `pyproject.toml` | `coding-standards.md` |\n    25|| Naming conventions and code patterns | Sample source files (5–10 per language) | `coding-standards.md` |\n    26|| Error handling and logging patterns | Source files | `coding-standards.md` |\n    27|| CI/CD pipeline and automation | `.github/workflows/`, `Jenkinsfile`, `.gitlab-ci.yml`, `Makefile` | `automation-standards.md` |\n    28|| Test frameworks and patterns | Test files, test config | `test-standards.md`, `automation-standards.md` |\n    29|| Architecture layers and module structure | Directory structure, import patterns | `arch-standards.md` |\n    30|| Security patterns | Auth middleware, secret handling, encryption usage | `security.md` |\n    31|| Environment configuration | `.env.example`, config files, environment variable usage | `env-config.md`, `config-management-rules.md` |\n    32|| Domain entities and business logic | Domain model files, service names, entity classes | `domain.md` |\n    33|| Constraints and non-negotiables | README, CONTRIBUTING, ADRs | `constraints.md` |\n    34|| Infrastructure topology and IaC | `Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.yml`, Terraform/Pulumi files, Kubernetes manifests, CI deploy steps | `infrastructure.md` |\n    35|| Build, test, lint, typecheck, security commands | `Makefile`, `package.json` scripts, `pyproject.toml`, CI pipeline definitions | `validation-tools.md` |\n    36|| Solution/project inventory, namespaces, project references, controllers, services, repositories | Root manifests (`*.sln`, `package.json`, workspace files), project files, top-level folders, representative type names | `project-inventory.md` |\n    37|| Codebase structure, bounded contexts, layer conventions, frontend/test layout, lookup hints | `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, source tree layout, representative files, test tree | `codebase-map.md` |\n    38|\n    39|## Documentation Analysis\n    40|\n    41|For each `*.pdf`/`*.md` in `artifacts/inputs/documentation/` (and any folded-in\n    42|`meeting-analysis.md`):\n    43|\n    44|| What to extract | Maps to context-pack file |\n    45||----------------|--------------------------|\n    46|| Domain glossary, business entities, terminology | `domain.md` |\n    47|| Architecture decisions and patterns | `arch-standards.md` |\n    48|| Technology choices and rationale | `tech-policy.md` |\n    49|| Security policies and requirements | `security.md` |\n    50|| Compliance and regulatory constraints | `constraints.md` |\n    51|| Customer background and business goals | `customer-background.md` |\n    52|| Testing requirements and quality gates | `test-standards.md` |\n    53|| Configuration and environment rules | `env-config.md`, `config-management-rules.md` |\n    54|| General best practices | `best-practices.md` |\n    55|\n</file>","isError":false}}
