{"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"toolu_01B81ThxkUQLMhLEdSsSQCXs","result":"<file path=\"artifacts/inputs/documentation/architecture/ARCH-SPEC.md\" lines=\"107\" start=\"1\" end=\"106\" returned=\"106\" has_more=\"true\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|# Architecture Specification - InsideFIFA-WEB\n     2|\n     3|## Service Catalog\n     4|\n     5|### SVC-001: Test Execution Service\n     6|**Name:** Test Execution Engine  \n     7|**Description:** Core service responsible for running web automation tests  \n     8|**Slices:** Test runner, Browser management, Test orchestration  \n     9|\n    10|### SVC-002: Page Object Service  \n    11|**Name:** Page Object Management  \n    12|**Description:** Manages page object models and element interactions  \n    13|**Slices:** Element locators, Page actions, Validation helpers  \n    14|\n    15|### SVC-003: Configuration Service  \n    16|**Name:** Test Configuration Management  \n    17|**Description:** Handles test data, environments, and language configurations  \n    18|**Slices:** Data loading, Environment switching, Language management  \n    19|\n    20|### SVC-004: Reporting Service  \n    21|**Name:** Test Results and Reporting  \n    22|**Description:** Generates test reports and captures execution metrics  \n    23|**Slices:** Report generation, Screenshot capture, Metrics collection  \n    24|\n    25|## Environment Definitions\n    26|\n    27|### ENV-001: Local Development\n    28|**Purpose:** Development and debugging of test cases  \n    29|**Scale:** Single machine  \n    30|**Browser:** Chrome desktop  \n    31|**Language:** English (en)  \n    32|\n    33|### ENV-002: CI/CD Pipeline\n    34|**Purpose:** Automated test execution in build pipeline  \n    35|**Scale:** Containerized environment  \n    36|**Browser:** Chrome headless  \n    37|**Language:** English (en)  \n    38|\n    39|### ENV-003: Staging Validation\n    40|**Purpose:** Pre-production validation against staging environment  \n    41|**Scale:** Cloud-based test environment  \n    42|**Browser:** Chrome desktop  \n    43|**Language:** English (en), Spanish (es), French (fr)  \n    44|\n    45|### ENV-004: Production Monitoring\n    46|**Purpose:** Production smoke tests and monitoring  \n    47|**Scale:** Production environment  \n    48|**Browser:** Chrome desktop  \n    49|**Language:** English (en)  \n    50|\n    51|## Integration Patterns\n    52|\n    53|### Pattern-001: Sequential Test Execution\n    54|**Description:** Tests run sequentially to avoid resource conflicts  \n    55|**Use Case:** Navigation testing where order matters  \n    56|\n    57|### Pattern-002: Parallel Test Execution\n    58|**Description:** Independent tests run in parallel for faster execution  \n    59|**Use Case:** Multi-language testing scenarios  \n    60|\n    61|### Pattern-003: Retry Mechanism\n    62|**Description:** Failed tests automatically retry with exponential backoff  \n    63|**Use Case:** Handling network instability and timing issues  \n    64|\n    65|## Deployment Strategy\n    66|\n    67|### Strategy: Containerized Test Execution\n    68|**Description:** Tests run in Docker containers for consistency across environments  \n    69|**Benefits:**\n    70|- Environment consistency\n    71|- Easy scaling\n    72|- Isolation from host system\n    73|- Simplified dependency management\n    74|\n    75|### CI/CD Integration\n    76|- GitHub Actions for test execution\n    77|- Automated test triggers on code changes\n    78|- Test result artifacts storage\n    79|- Failure notification system\n    80|\n    81|## Technology Stack\n    82|\n    83|| Component | Technology | Version |\n    84||-----------|------------|---------|\n    85|| Automation Framework | Playwright | 1.40+ |\n    86|| Programming Language | TypeScript | 5.0+ |\n    87|| Package Manager | npm | 10.0+ |\n    88|| Container Platform | Docker | 24.0+ |\n    89|| CI/CD Platform | GitHub Actions | Latest |\n    90|| Reporting | Playwright HTML Reporter | 1.40+ |\n    91|\n    92|## Quality Gates\n    93|\n    94|### Gate-001: Code Quality\n    95|- TypeScript compilation without errors\n    96|- ESLint compliance\n    97|- Code coverage > 80%\n    98|\n    99|### Gate-002: Test Execution\n   100|- All tests pass in local environment\n   101|- Performance benchmarks met\n   102|- No critical test failures\n   103|\n   104|### Gate-003: Deployment Readiness\n   105|- Tests pass in CI/CD pipeline\n   106|- Staging environment validation successful\n</file>","isError":false}}
