{"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"toolu_017Y3UNiJQ4wcKcHwsrj9EHw","result":"<file path=\"/Users/andres.mesa/.ai_pods_stepwise/registry/skills/tech-blueprints/blueprints/_tech-stack-selection.template.md\" lines=\"78\" start=\"1\" end=\"78\" returned=\"78\" has_more=\"false\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|# Tech Stack Selection\n     2|\n     3|<!--\n     4|COPY this file to `./artifacts/inputs/tech-stack-selection.md` in the project repo and fill it\n     5|in. Produced by the `collect-client-info` gate, consumed by `analyze-context-pack-inputs`.\n     6|\n     7|This file is AUTHORITATIVE over the blueprint library. Blueprints not listed under\n     8|\"Selected blueprints\" are OUT OF SCOPE for this project and must not contribute rules to the\n     9|context pack, even if they are physically present in artifacts/inputs/.\n    10|\n    11|Exactly ONE L1 platform. Blueprints from two L1 platforms carry mutually exclusive mandates\n    12|(one requires CDK, another Terraform, another Helm) and the analyzer has no authority to\n    13|choose between them.\n    14|-->\n    15|\n    16|## Selected blueprints\n    17|\n    18|List the `blueprint_id` of each selected blueprint. Ids are declared in each blueprint's\n    19|`§14 Normative Profile`.\n    20|\n    21|| Layer | blueprint_id | Why selected |\n    22||---|---|---|\n    23|| L1 (exactly one) | `<aws\\|azure\\|gcp\\|oracle\\|ovh\\|vercel\\|cloudflare>` | `<binding constraint>` |\n    24|| L2 | `<google-app-stack\\|mobile-native\\|…>` | `<…>` |\n    25|| L2 | | |\n    26|| L3 | `<agent-architecture-principles\\|langgraph\\|google-agent-stack\\|vendor-agent-sdks>` | `<…>` |\n    27|| L4 | `security-baseline` | Always selected |\n    28|| L4 | `pre-ship-checklist` | Always selected |\n    29|\n    30|`security-baseline` and `pre-ship-checklist` are **always selected**. Remove them only with a\n    31|recorded exception.\n    32|\n    33|If the project has an agentic component, `agent-architecture-principles` is **required**\n    34|alongside whichever framework or runtime blueprint is chosen — the framework blueprints assume\n    35|its vocabulary.\n    36|\n    37|## Binding constraint\n    38|\n    39|One or two sentences: what actually drove the L1 selection. See `00-choosing-a-platform.md §5`.\n    40|\n    41|> `<e.g. \"European data residency is contractual; OVHcloud selected for sovereignty and zero\n    42|> egress. Team has Kubernetes capability in-house.\">`\n    43|\n    44|## Accepted trade-offs\n    45|\n    46|The \"When Not to Choose\" section of each selected blueprint lists where that platform loses.\n    47|Record which of those the project is knowingly accepting — this is what stops them being\n    48|rediscovered as defects later.\n    49|\n    50|- `<e.g. \"Azure has no managed mobile offline sync; offline is a degradation mode, not a\n    51|  requirement. Accepted.\">`\n    52|- `<…>`\n    53|\n    54|## Deviations from blueprint mandates\n    55|\n    56|Any `§10` playbook maxim or `§14` rule this project will NOT follow, with justification.\n    57|Anything listed here **overrides** the blueprint and is what the context pack must reflect.\n    58|\n    59|| Blueprint | Rule being overridden | Justification |\n    60||---|---|---|\n    61|| `<id>` | `<rule text or §ref>` | `<why>` |\n    62|\n    63|Leave empty if there are none. An empty table is a meaningful statement, not an unfilled one.\n    64|\n    65|## Project-specific resolutions\n    66|\n    67|The blueprints end with `open_questions` that only the project can answer. Resolve the ones\n    68|that apply; unresolved items flow through to the context pack's `## Open Questions`.\n    69|\n    70|| Question (from blueprint `open_questions`) | Resolution |\n    71||---|---|\n    72|| `<question>` | `<answer, or \"unresolved\">` |\n    73|\n    74|## Not covered here\n    75|\n    76|`domain.md` and `customer-background.md` derive from project and customer inputs — the project\n    77|brief, requirements, transcripts, and source code — not from this file or from any blueprint.\n    78|\n</file>","isError":false}}
